# The Lagrangian-variables Navier-Stokes Hamiltonian derived FROM the Eulerian one,
# carrying the incompressibility constraint through every step.
#
# Run:  cadabra2-cli -q -n docs/ns_lagrangian_hamiltonian.cdb
# (Cadabra 2.5.x from the pinned nixpkgs named in docs/VERIFY_QG_DENSITIZED.md:
#  nix build "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/b5aa0fbd538984f6e3d201be0005b4463d8b09f8#cadabra2"
#  or `nix develop` in this repository; see docs/VERIFY_FARIS_LAVINE_N.md.)
#
# What this module derives.  The plan of record (../timepiece/CONSOLIDATED_PLAN.md,
# section "Plan items -- Navier-Stokes, Eulerian and Lagrangian", items 1-6 and 9,
# and the 2026-09-25 landed wave) defines the SAME fluid in two variable pictures:
#
#   EULERIAN (starting point):
#     the residual  R_i = sum_j u_j u_{i,j} + q_i - nu w_i   (ChapterNavierStokesFullEulerianFock,
#       nsResPoly), the incompressibility constraint  div u = sum_j u_{j,j} = 0  whose
#       Lagrange multiplier is the pressure p (docs/ns_pressure_constraint.cdb: second-class,
#       SOLVED for, not gauged), and the elimination of the jet variables by the spatial
#       Fourier transform  u_{i,j} -> i k_j u_i,  w_i -> -|k|^2 u_i,  q_i -> i k_i p
#       (CONSOLIDATED_PLAN.md item 6 / note section 5.1; products-with-derivatives are
#       disposed of by the MOMENTUM-SPACE CONVOLUTION, the NS-and-QG-only device of
#       BookProof/ChapterNsAdvectionConvolution).
#
#   LAGRANGIAN (target): trajectories X(a,t), velocity v = d_t X, deformation gradient
#     F = grad_a X, velocity gradient V, viscous coordinate S.  In this picture the
#     constraint is transported by CAUCHY's Jacobian theorem to the exact form
#         volumePoly = det F - 1 = 0          (ChapterNavierStokesFullLagrangianFock,
#         "the exact incompressibility constraint in Lagrangian variables"),
#     the momentum equation is the residual
#         lagResPoly: R_i = acc_i + sum_j cof(F)_{ji} q_j - S_i   (acceleration + Piola
#         pressure - viscous coordinate), and the one-parcel canonical Hamiltonian is
#         h = 1/2 sum P^2 + nu sum Q^2 + sum f.P + constraintOp          (lagCanData,
#         ChapterNavierStokesLagrangianCanonical; constraintOp = 0 in the canonical model,
#         cf. NS_LAGRANGIAN_OUTER_FOCK_ESA.md section 1), the operator of
#         nsLagrangian_timeIndependent_singleTime.  The FINAL Hamiltonian is the enclosure
#         H = dGamma(h) = sum_ij h_ij C^dag(e_i) A(e_j)  (creation LEFT, annihilation
#         RIGHT), ESA on the finite-parcel core by ChapterNsLagrangianOuterFockEsa
#         (lagOne_dGamma_esa) and, for the interacting auxiliary sum of squares, by
#         ChapterNsFullLagrangianFockEsa (lagFullFockHam_esa / lagSectorHam_esa = weylPoly).
#
# The derivation, in four steps, each machine-checked below:
#   E  the Eulerian residual and constraint in momentum space (CHECK 1-2);
#   J  the constraint TRANSPORTS: d(det F)/dt = det F * div u (Jacobi's identity,
#      CHECK 3), so div u = 0 <=> det F = 1 with F(0) = I (CHECK 4), and the linear
#      part of volumePoly is exactly the displacement divergence (CHECK 5);
#   M  the material substitution (note section 6: sigma(F_ij) = i l_j xi_i, sigma(S_i)
#      = -|l|^2 v_i): the constraint DEGENERATES under it -- all nine cofactors vanish,
#      det F |-> 0, volumePoly |-> -1, volumePoly^2 |-> 1, the Piola pressure dies
#      (CHECK 6-8) -- which is WHY det F must ride as an INDEPENDENT scalar mode with
#      the penalty V_kappa = kappa (det F - 1)^2 (ChapterNsLagrangianDetFarisLavine,
#      NsLagrangianDetFL), and what survives is the eliminated material momentum
#      equation  sigma(R_i) = a_i + |l|^2 v_i  (CHECK 9, lagElimSubst_lagResPoly);
#   C  the one-parcel canonical Hamiltonian: the CCR [P,Q] = -i (CHECK 11), the
#      oscillator identity 1/2 P^2 + nu Q^2 = omega (N + 3/2), omega = sqrt(2 nu)
#      (CHECK 12), the completed square behind the Kato-Rellich drift and the spectral
#      shift -1/2 |f|^2 (CHECK 13), the Heisenberg equations d<Q>/dt = <P> + f,
#      d<P>/dt = -2 nu <Q> at frequency omega (CHECK 14), the enclosure's number
#      conservation and lift identity (CHECK 15), and the sextic degree of the penalty
#      form V_kappa (CHECK 16).
#
# Engine conventions (learned from the engine, cf. docs/VERIFY_QG_DENSITIZED.md and
# ../AGENTS.md): scalar names are declared ::Symbol, ladder names ::NonCommuting, no
# handle name carries an underscore or starts with `det`, handles inserted inside an
# expression go through @(...), and every check prints its value with 0 expected
# (labels marked "expect 1" print 1).  The CCR rewrite set follows
# docs/ns_kvn_equation.cdb.  3x3 index pairs are spelled with letters: a=0, b=1, c=2.
#
# Numerical counterpart: fock_sirk/tests/ns_lagrangian_validation.rs runs the same
# structure on the nested Fock space (SIRK/Hashimoto), including the penalty family
# H_kappa = 1/2 sum P^2 + nu sum Q^2 + kappa volumePoly^2.

# ===========================================================================
# declarations
# ===========================================================================
i::ImaginaryI.
{Faa, Fab, Fac, Fba, Fbb, Fbc, Fca, Fcb, Fcc}::Symbol.
{duaa, duab, duac, duba, dubb, dubc, duca, ducb, ducc}::Symbol.
{ua, ub, uc, ka, kb, kc, p, qa, qb, qc, wa, nu, t}::Symbol.
{xia, xib, xic, lla, llb, llc, va, vb, vc, sa, sb, sc}::Symbol.
{pa, pb, pc, mata, matb, matc}::Symbol.
{fa, fb, fc, om, kappa, eaa, eab, eac, eba, ebb, ebc, eca, ecb, ecc}::Symbol.
{haa, hab, hba, hbb}::Symbol.
{a1, ad1, a2, ad2, a3, ad3}::NonCommuting.

# ---- local reduction helper (the cli has no built-in clean/diff; cf. the
# ---- def clean of docs/ns_pressure_poisson.cdb) --------------------------------
# sort_product (CLI builtin, the one docs/ns_kvn_equation.cdb calls) puts every
# product into a canonical factor order, so structurally equal terms written with
# different factor order cancel under collect_terms.  Engine trap learned here:
# hand-built swap rules of the form "b a -> a b" fed to substitute(...,
# repeat=True) DO NOT TERMINATE in this CLI -- the commutative matcher re-fires
# on its own output forever -- so ordering is delegated to sort_product, and
# only the non-commutative ccr/cross rewrites (whose rules cannot re-match their
# own output) go through substitute with repeat=True.
def tidy(ex, depth=1):
    distribute(ex)
    for _ in range(depth):
        product_rule(ex)
        distribute(ex)
    sort_product(ex)
    distribute(ex)
    canonicalise(ex)
    collect_terms(ex)
    return ex

# ===========================================================================
# E. the Eulerian starting point, in momentum space, in momentum space
# ===========================================================================
print("== E. Eulerian residual and constraint, after the spatial-Fourier elimination ==");

# CHECK 1: the residual symbol.  R_a = sum_y u_y u_{a,y} + q_a - nu w_a with the
# elimination u_{a,y} -> i k_y u_a,  q_a -> i k_a p,  w_a -> -|k|^2 u_a must give
# sigma(R_a) = i u_a (k.u) + i k_a p + nu |k|^2 u_a.
ra0 = Ex(r"ua*duaa + ub*duab + uc*duac + qa - nu*wa");
substitute(ra0, Ex(r"duaa -> I*ka*ua, duab -> I*kb*ua, duac -> I*kc*ua"), repeat=True);
substitute(ra0, Ex(r"qa -> I*ka*p, wa -> - (ka*ka + kb*kb + kc*kc) * ua"), repeat=True);
tidy(ra0);
raexp = Ex(r"I*ua*(ka*ua + kb*ub + kc*uc) + I*ka*p + nu*(ka*ka + kb*kb + kc*kc)*ua");
chk1 := @(ra0) - @(raexp);
tidy(chk1);
print("CHECK 1  NSLAG sigma(R_a) = i u_a (k.u) + i k_a p + nu |k|^2 u_a (0 = ok):", chk1);

# CHECK 2: the constraint in momentum space.  div u = u_{a,a} + u_{b,b} + u_{c,c}
# |-> i (k.u): a LINEAR form in the modes; its surface is k.u = 0.  (That the pressure
# p is its second-class multiplier, solved by p = -S/|k|^2, is certified in
# docs/ns_pressure_constraint.cdb CHECK 1-5 -- not re-derived here.)
div0 = Ex(r"duaa + dubb + ducc");
substitute(div0, Ex(r"duaa -> I*ka*ua, dubb -> I*kb*ub, ducc -> I*kc*uc"), repeat=True);
tidy(div0);
print("CHECK 2  NSLAG div u |-> i (k.u), the linear constraint symbol:", div0);

# ===========================================================================
# J. the constraint transports: div u = 0 <=> det F = 1
# ===========================================================================
print("== J. Cauchy transport of the constraint into material variables ==");

# the signed cofactors of F (the Lean cofPoly convention: C_xy = (-1)^{x+y} minor_xy,
# verified identical to BookProof.ChapterNavierStokesFullLagrangianFock.cofPoly's
# first-row expansion in DESIGN_COMPARISON_N_20260915.cdb A1/A2)
cfaa = Ex(r"Fbb*Fcc - Fbc*Fcb");
cfab = Ex(r"-(Fba*Fcc - Fbc*Fca)");
cfac = Ex(r"Fba*Fcb - Fbb*Fca");
cfba = Ex(r"-(Fab*Fcc - Fac*Fcb)");
cfbb = Ex(r"Faa*Fcc - Fac*Fca");
cfbc = Ex(r"-(Faa*Fcb - Fab*Fca)");
cfca = Ex(r"Fab*Fbc - Fac*Fbb");
cfcb = Ex(r"-(Faa*Fbc - Fac*Fba)");
cfcc = Ex(r"Faa*Fbb - Fab*Fba");

# volumePoly = detPoly - 1 (Lean: detPoly is the first-row expansion, volumePoly = detPoly - 1)
volpoly = Ex(r"Faa*(Fbb*Fcc - Fbc*Fcb) - Fab*(Fba*Fcc - Fbc*Fca) + Fac*(Fba*Fcb - Fbb*Fca) - 1");

# CHECK 3: Jacobi's identity for the flow map: with Fdot_xy = sum_z du_xz F_zy
# (d/dt X_x(a) = u_x(X(a)) differentiated in a),  d(det F)/dt = sum_xy C_xy Fdot_xy
# must equal det F * div u = det F * sum_x du_xx.
fdotaa = Ex(r"duaa*Faa + duab*Fba + duac*Fca");
fdotab = Ex(r"duaa*Fab + duab*Fbb + duac*Fcb");
fdotac = Ex(r"duaa*Fac + duab*Fbc + duac*Fcc");
fdotba = Ex(r"duba*Faa + dubb*Fba + dubc*Fca");
fdotbb = Ex(r"duba*Fab + dubb*Fbb + dubc*Fcb");
fdotbc = Ex(r"duba*Fac + dubb*Fbc + dubc*Fcc");
fdotca = Ex(r"duca*Faa + ducb*Fba + ducc*Fca");
fdotcb = Ex(r"duca*Fab + ducb*Fbb + ducc*Fcb");
fdotcc = Ex(r"duca*Fac + ducb*Fbc + ducc*Fcc");
jacobi := @(cfaa)*@(fdotaa) + @(cfab)*@(fdotab) + @(cfac)*@(fdotac)        + @(cfba)*@(fdotba) + @(cfbb)*@(fdotbb) + @(cfbc)*@(fdotbc)        + @(cfca)*@(fdotca) + @(cfcb)*@(fdotcb) + @(cfcc)*@(fdotcc);
rhsjac := (1 + @(volpoly)) * (duaa + dubb + ducc);
chk3 := @(jacobi) - @(rhsjac);
tidy(chk3);
print("CHECK 3  NSLAG d(det F)/dt - det F * div u = 0   (Cauchy, 0 = ok):", chk3);

# CHECK 4: at F = I the constraint surface is exactly det F = 1 (volumePoly = 0),
# i.e. the Eulerian constraint div u = 0 and the material constraint det F = 1 agree
# on the initial slice where the flow map starts as the identity.
volI := @(volpoly);
substitute(volI, Ex(r"Faa -> 1, Fab -> 0, Fac -> 0, Fba -> 0, Fbb -> 1, Fbc -> 0, Fca -> 0, Fcb -> 0, Fcc -> 1"), repeat=True);
tidy(volI);
print("CHECK 4  NSLAG volumePoly at F = I               (0 = ok):", volI);

# CHECK 5: the exact expansion of the constraint at F = I + t E:
#   vol(I + t E) = t tr(E) + t^2 (principal 2x2 minors of E) + t^3 det(E).
# The linear part is the displacement divergence and the quadratic part the
# minors (read off by inspection); the module verifies the stronger full
# expansion directly, since the cli provides no scalar diff().
volit := @(volpoly);
substitute(volit, Ex(r"Faa -> 1 + t*eaa, Fbb -> 1 + t*ebb, Fcc -> 1 + t*ecc"), repeat=True);
substitute(volit, Ex(r"Fab -> t*eab, Fac -> t*eac, Fba -> t*eba, Fbc -> t*ebc, Fca -> t*eca, Fcb -> t*ecb"), repeat=True);
tidy(volit);
chk5 := @(volit) - ( t*(eaa + ebb + ecc) + t*t*(eaa*ebb - eab*eba + eaa*ecc - eac*eca + ebb*ecc - ebc*ecb) + t*t*t*(eaa*(ebb*ecc - ebc*ecb) - eab*(eba*ecc - ebc*eca) + eac*(eba*ecb - ebb*eca)) );
tidy(chk5); collect_terms(chk5);
print("CHECK 5  NSLAG vol(I+tE) = t trE + t^2 minors + t^3 detE (0 = ok):", chk5);

# ===========================================================================
# M. the material substitution: what survives, what degenerates
# ===========================================================================
print("== M. material substitution (note section 6): F_ij -> i l_j xi_i, S_i -> -|l|^2 v_i ==");

rank1 = Ex(r"Faa -> I*lla*xia, Fbb -> I*llb*xib, Fcc -> I*llc*xic, Fab -> I*llb*xia, Fac -> I*llc*xia, Fba -> I*lla*xib, Fbc -> I*llc*xib, Fca -> I*lla*xic, Fcb -> I*llb*xic");

# CHECK 6: all nine cofactors vanish on the rank-one substitution (every 2x2 minor
# of a rank-one matrix is zero) -- cof(F) = 0, the finding of CONSOLIDATED_PLAN.md
# item 6 (rankOne_cof_zero, B4a-B4d of DESIGN_COMPARISON_N_20260915.cdb).
minsq := @(cfaa)^2 + @(cfab)^2 + @(cfac)^2 + @(cfba)^2 + @(cfbb)^2 + @(cfbc)^2        + @(cfca)^2 + @(cfcb)^2 + @(cfcc)^2;
substitute(minsq, rank1, repeat=True);
tidy(minsq);
print("CHECK 6  NSLAG sum of squares of all cofactors under F = i l (x) xi (0 = ok):", minsq);

# CHECK 7: the constraint DEGENERATES under the elimination -- det F |-> 0, hence
# volumePoly |-> -1 and volumePoly^2 |-> 1: a constant with no field content that
# cannot couple to the field (lagElimSubst_volumePoly / _volumePoly_sq, B5/B5b).
volk := @(volpoly);
substitute(volk, rank1, repeat=True);
tidy(volk);
print("CHECK 7a NSLAG volumePoly |-> det F - 1 under the rank-one map (expect -1):", volk);
volk2 := @(volpoly) * @(volpoly);
substitute(volk2, rank1, repeat=True);
tidy(volk2);
print("CHECK 7b NSLAG volumePoly^2 under the rank-one map (expect 1):", volk2);

# CHECK 8: the Piola pressure term dies with the cofactors (lagElimSubst_piola):
# the ENTIRE pressure coupling of the material momentum equation vanishes.
# Component b of lagResPoly's pressure part: sum_j cof(F)_{j b} q_j.
piolab := @(cfab)*pa + @(cfbb)*pb + @(cfcb)*pc;
substitute(piolab, rank1, repeat=True);
tidy(piolab);
print("CHECK 8  NSLAG Piola term sum_j cof(F)_{jb} q_j |-> 0 (0 = ok):", piolab);

# CHECK 9: what SURVIVES is the eliminated material momentum equation
#   sigma(R_b) = mat_b + |l|^2 v_b      (lagElimSubst_lagResPoly):
# lagResPoly R_b = mat_b + sum_j cof_{jb} q_j - S_b, with cof |-> 0 (CHECK 6/8) and
# sigma(S_b) = -|l|^2 v_b: no pressure, acceleration plus viscous term.
rb0 := matb + @(cfab)*pa + @(cfbb)*pb + @(cfcb)*pc - sb;
substitute(rb0, Ex(r"sb -> - (lla*lla + llb*llb + llc*llc) * vb"), repeat=True);
substitute(rb0, rank1, repeat=True);
tidy(rb0);
rbexp = Ex(r"matb + (lla*lla + llb*llb + llc*llc) * vb");
chk9 := @(rb0) - @(rbexp);
tidy(chk9);
print("CHECK 9  NSLAG eliminated material residual = a_b + |l|^2 v_b (0 = ok):", chk9);

# Reading (the reason the derivation needs the penalty): the elimination maps the
# constraint to the constant -1 (CHECK 7), so det F is kept as an INDEPENDENT scalar
# mode and the constraint rides in the Hamiltonian as the squared penalty form
#     V_kappa = kappa (det F - 1)^2,
# exactly the V_kappa of BookProof/ChapterNsLagrangianDetFarisLavine (NsLagrangianDetFL)
# and one of the squared forms of lagSectorHam (weylPoly: 1/2 sum pi^2 + 1/2 sum form^2).

# ===========================================================================
# C. the one-parcel canonical Hamiltonian
# ===========================================================================
print("== C. the canonical one-parcel Hamiltonian h = 1/2 sum P^2 + nu sum Q^2 + sum f.P ==");
print("     (omega = sqrt(2 nu); Q = (a+a^dag)/sqrt(2 omega), P = i sqrt(omega/2) (a^dag - a);");
print("     the ladder algebra is shown at the package instance omega = 1, nu = 1/2;");
print("     CHECK 12 carries the general omega = sqrt(2 nu))");

# ladder handles at omega = 1: P_m = i (ad_m - a_m)/sqrt(2), Q_m = (ad_m + a_m)/sqrt(2)
Pa = Ex(r"I*(ad1 - a1)/sqrt(2)");
Pb = Ex(r"I*(ad2 - a2)/sqrt(2)");
Pc = Ex(r"I*(ad3 - a3)/sqrt(2)");
Qa = Ex(r"(ad1 + a1)/sqrt(2)");
Qb = Ex(r"(ad2 + a2)/sqrt(2)");
Qc = Ex(r"(ad3 + a3)/sqrt(2)");

ccr = Ex(r"a1 ad1 -> ad1 a1 + 1, a2 ad2 -> ad2 a2 + 1, a3 ad3 -> ad3 a3 + 1");
cross = Ex(r"a1 ad2 -> ad2 a1, a1 ad3 -> ad3 a1, a2 ad1 -> ad1 a2, a2 ad3 -> ad3 a2, a3 ad1 -> ad1 a3, a3 ad2 -> ad2 a3, a1 a2 -> a2 a1, a1 a3 -> a3 a1, a2 a3 -> a3 a2, ad1 ad2 -> ad2 ad1, ad1 ad3 -> ad3 ad1, ad2 ad3 -> ad3 ad2");

# numeric folding: the engine NEVER evaluates I*I -> -1 or sqrt(x)^2 -> x on
# its own, so those factors must be rewritten explicitly or the rational/I
# prefactors of the ladder algebra can never cancel.  Engine traps learned:
# a rule with a numeric prefactor on the lhs is rejected ((2 om)**(-1) om must
# be written om**(-1) om, since (2 om)**(-1) normalises to (1/2) om**(-1)), and
# a self-referential rule like Faa -> t*Faa must run WITHOUT repeat=True.
numfold = Ex(r"I I -> -1, (sqrt(2))**(-1) (sqrt(2))**(-1) -> 1/2, sqrt(1/2 om) sqrt(1/2 om) -> 1/2 om, (sqrt(2*om))**(-1) (sqrt(2*om))**(-1) -> (2 om)**(-1), om**(-1) om -> 1");

# normal-order a commutator check: expand FIRST (the ccr/cross patterns only
# match once the products are distributed), rewrite the CCR, fold numerics,
# then tidy.  (substitute before distribute was the original bug: the rules
# silently matched nothing.)
def norder(ex):
    distribute(ex); distribute(ex); distribute(ex);
    # alternate ccr and cross to a JOINT fixpoint: cross moves a's past ad's
    # and can create fresh a ad adjacencies that ccr must still rewrite
    # (one ccr pass followed by one cross pass leaves cubic residue).
    for _ in range(4):
        substitute(ex, ccr, repeat=True); distribute(ex);
        substitute(ex, cross, repeat=True); distribute(ex);
    substitute(ex, numfold, repeat=True);
    tidy(ex); canonicalise(ex);
    return ex

# CHECK 11: the CCR [P_i, Q_j] = -i delta_ij (comm_lagP_lagQ).
cca := @(Pa)*@(Qa) - @(Qa)*@(Pa) + I;
norder(cca);
print("CHECK 11a NSLAG [P_a, Q_a] + i = 0                    (0 = ok):", cca);
ccb := @(Pb)*@(Qb) - @(Qb)*@(Pb) + I;
norder(ccb);
print("CHECK 11b NSLAG [P_b, Q_b] + i = 0                    (0 = ok):", ccb);
ccc := @(Pc)*@(Qc) - @(Qc)*@(Pc) + I;
norder(ccc);
print("CHECK 11c NSLAG [P_c, Q_c] + i = 0                    (0 = ok):", ccc);
ccx := @(Pa)*@(Qb) - @(Qb)*@(Pa) + @(Pa)*@(Qc) - @(Qc)*@(Pa)      + @(Pb)*@(Qa) - @(Qa)*@(Pb) + @(Pb)*@(Qc) - @(Qc)*@(Pb)      + @(Pc)*@(Qa) - @(Qa)*@(Pc) + @(Pc)*@(Qb) - @(Qb)*@(Pc);
norder(ccx);
print("CHECK 11d NSLAG sum_{i != j} [P_i, Q_j] = 0           (0 = ok):", ccx);

# CHECK 12: the oscillator identity 1/2 sum P^2 + nu sum Q^2 = omega (N + 3/2),
# omega = sqrt(2 nu) encoded as nu -> om^2/2  (lagCan_secondOrder_eq / lagT_eq_number).
Pl1 = Ex(r"I*sqrt(om/2)*(ad1 - a1)");
Pl2 = Ex(r"I*sqrt(om/2)*(ad2 - a2)");
Pl3 = Ex(r"I*sqrt(om/2)*(ad3 - a3)");
Ql1 = Ex(r"(ad1 + a1)/sqrt(2*om)");
Ql2 = Ex(r"(ad2 + a2)/sqrt(2*om)");
Ql3 = Ex(r"(ad3 + a3)/sqrt(2*om)");
tosc := 1/2*@(Pl1)*@(Pl1) + nu*@(Ql1)*@(Ql1)       + 1/2*@(Pl2)*@(Pl2) + nu*@(Ql2)*@(Ql2)       + 1/2*@(Pl3)*@(Pl3) + nu*@(Ql3)*@(Ql3);
substitute(tosc, Ex(r"nu -> om*om/2"), repeat=True);
tidy(tosc);
chk12 := @(tosc) - om*(ad1*a1 + ad2*a2 + ad3*a3) - 3*om/2;
norder(chk12);
print("CHECK 12 NSLAG 1/2 sum P^2 + nu sum Q^2 - omega (N + 3/2) = 0 (0 = ok):", chk12);

# CHECK 13: the completed-square expansion behind h + 1/2 |f|^2 = 1/2 sum (P_m+f_m)^2
# + nu sum Q^2 (the Kato-Rellich input hFull = kinetic + viscous + drift + constraintOp,
# and the source of the exact spectral shift -1/2 |f|^2 in ns_lagrangian_validation.rs):
#   1/2 (P_m + f_m)^2 - 1/2 P_m^2 - f_m P_m - 1/2 f_m^2 = 0  for each m.
Ppfa := @(Pa) + fa;
Ppfb := @(Pb) + fb;
Ppfc := @(Pc) + fc;
chk13 := 1/2*@(Ppfa)*@(Ppfa) - 1/2*@(Pa)*@(Pa) - fa*@(Pa) - 1/2*fa*fa        + 1/2*@(Ppfb)*@(Ppfb) - 1/2*@(Pb)*@(Pb) - fb*@(Pb) - 1/2*fb*fb        + 1/2*@(Ppfc)*@(Ppfc) - 1/2*@(Pc)*@(Pc) - fc*@(Pc) - 1/2*fc*fc;
tidy(chk13); canonicalise(chk13);
print("CHECK 13 NSLAG 1/2 (P+f)^2 - 1/2 P^2 - f P - 1/2 f^2 = 0 (0 = ok):", chk13);

# CHECK 14: the Heisenberg equations of the derived Hamiltonian (omega = 1, nu = 1/2
# instance):  d<Q_m>/dt = i[H, Q_m] = P_m + f_m,  d<P_m>/dt = i[H, P_m] = -2 nu Q_m.
Hh := 1/2*@(Pa)*@(Pa) + 1/2*@(Qa)*@(Qa) + fa*@(Pa)     + 1/2*@(Pb)*@(Pb) + 1/2*@(Qb)*@(Qb) + fb*@(Pb)     + 1/2*@(Pc)*@(Pc) + 1/2*@(Qc)*@(Qc) + fc*@(Pc);
Im = Ex(r"I");
eq14a := I * (@(Hh)*@(Qa) - @(Qa)*@(Hh)) - (@(Pa) + fa);
norder(eq14a);
print("CHECK 14a NSLAG i[H,Q_a] - (P_a + f_a) = 0           (0 = ok):", eq14a);
eq14b := I * (@(Hh)*@(Qb) - @(Qb)*@(Hh)) - (@(Pb) + fb);
norder(eq14b);
print("CHECK 14b NSLAG i[H,Q_b] - (P_b + f_b) = 0           (0 = ok):", eq14b);
eq14c := I * (@(Hh)*@(Qc) - @(Qc)*@(Hh)) - (@(Pc) + fc);
norder(eq14c);
print("CHECK 14c NSLAG i[H,Q_c] - (P_c + f_c) = 0           (0 = ok):", eq14c);
eq14d := I * (@(Hh)*@(Pa) - @(Pa)*@(Hh)) + @(Qa);
norder(eq14d);
print("CHECK 14d NSLAG i[H,P_a] + 2 nu Q_a = 0 (nu = 1/2)   (0 = ok):", eq14d);
eq14e := I * (@(Hh)*@(Pb) - @(Pb)*@(Hh)) + @(Qb);
norder(eq14e);
print("CHECK 14e NSLAG i[H,P_b] + 2 nu Q_b = 0 (nu = 1/2)   (0 = ok):", eq14e);
eq14f := I * (@(Hh)*@(Pc) - @(Pc)*@(Hh)) + @(Qc);
norder(eq14f);
print("CHECK 14f NSLAG i[H,P_c] + 2 nu Q_c = 0 (nu = 1/2)   (0 = ok):", eq14f);

# CHECK 15: the FINAL Hamiltonian is the enclosure H = dGamma(h) = sum h_ij ad_i a_j
# (creation LEFT, annihilation RIGHT).  Two structural facts:
#   15a  [dGamma(h), N] = 0  -- parcel number is conserved (dGamma_inSector /
#        nsSpDGamma_number_conserving);
#   15b  [dGamma(h), ad_1] = sum_i h_{i1} ad_i  -- the lift acts one-particle-wise
#        (the identity behind lagOne_dGamma_esa).
DG = Ex(r"haa*ad1*a1 + hab*ad1*a2 + hba*ad2*a1 + hbb*ad2*a2");
Nop = Ex(r"ad1*a1 + ad2*a2");
chk15a := @(DG)*@(Nop) - @(Nop)*@(DG);
norder(chk15a);
print("CHECK 15a NSLAG [dGamma(h), N] = 0                   (0 = ok):", chk15a);
chk15b := @(DG)*ad1 - ad1*@(DG) - (haa*ad1 + hba*ad2);
norder(chk15b);
print("CHECK 15b NSLAG [dGamma(h), ad_1] - sum_i h_i1 ad_i (0 = ok):", chk15b);

# CHECK 16: the penalty form V_kappa = kappa (det F - 1)^2 is SEXTIC in F
# (the B3 degree check of DESIGN_COMPARISON_N_20260915.cdb, here derived by scaling
# F |-> t F:  volumePoly(t F) = t^3 det F - 1, so its square is
# t^6 (det F)^2 - 2 t^3 (det F) + 1).
volk3 := @(volpoly) * @(volpoly);
# single pass on purpose: the scaling rules re-introduce their own lhs symbol,
# so repeat=True would loop forever (verified).
substitute(volk3, Ex(r"Faa -> t*Faa, Fab -> t*Fab, Fac -> t*Fac, Fba -> t*Fba, Fbb -> t*Fbb, Fbc -> t*Fbc, Fca -> t*Fca, Fcb -> t*Fcb, Fcc -> t*Fcc"));
tidy(volk3);
deth := @(volpoly) + 1;
chk16 := @(volk3) - (@(deth) * t*t*t - 1) * (@(deth) * t*t*t - 1);
tidy(chk16); collect_terms(chk16);
print("CHECK 16 NSLAG (det(tF) - 1)^2 = (t^3 det F - 1)^2    (0 = ok):", chk16);

print("== summary ==");
print("Eulerian  H = sum_i {pi_i, A_i}, A_i = sum_j u_j u_{i,j} + q_i - nu u_{i,jj}, div u = 0");
print("  -> transported constraint (CHECK 3-5):   det F - 1 = 0");
print("  -> material substitution (CHECK 6-9):    surviving residual a_i + |l|^2 v_i,");
print("     constraint degenerate => det F independent mode + V_kappa = kappa (det F - 1)^2");
print("  -> one-parcel h (CHECK 11-14):           1/2 sum P^2 + nu sum Q^2 + sum f.P,");
print("     [P,Q] = -i,  1/2 P^2 + nu Q^2 = omega (N + 3/2),  Heisenberg at omega = sqrt(2 nu)");
print("  -> final Hamiltonian (CHECK 15):         H = dGamma(h), creation left, annihilation");
print("     right, number conserving; penalty rides as V_kappa (CHECK 16, sextic)");
